---
description: Module pattern — 6-point wiring, inline opt-in. Applies when editing modules anywhere.
globs:
  - studio/schemas/objects/modules/**
  - web/src/components/modules/**
  - web/sanity/queries/components/modules/**
---

A **module** is a paired Sanity object (`module.<id>`) plus a React component (`Module<Name>.tsx`). `pnpm gen:module <Name>` scaffolds one and wires all **6 points**; `pnpm check:wiring` compares them exactly:

1. `studio/schemas/objects/modules/module<Name>.ts` — `defineType`, `name: "module.<id>"`, fields, `preview`, optional `icon`.
2. `studio/schemas/index.ts` — import + add to `schemaTypes`.
3. `studio/schemas/fields/modulesArrayField.ts` — append `{ type: "module.<id>" }` to `moduleTypes`.
4. `web/src/components/modules/Module<Name>.tsx` — `module: ModuleOf<"module.<id>">`, accepts `{ module, locale, siteLocale }`. No `data-sanity` in the component — `ModulesRenderer` wraps every module with it.
5. `web/src/components/modules/ModulesRenderer.tsx` — `case "module.<id>":` in `renderModuleChild()` (the `never` fallback makes a missing case a `tsc` error).
6. `web/sanity/queries/components/modules/<name>.ts` — `module<Name>Query` projection, full i18n arrays, listed in `modulesQuery`.

Then `pnpm generate` and commit the generated files. Inline use in rich text is **opt-in** and takes three more places, all or none (`--inline` does it): Studio `richTextMedia.ts` `of`, `richTextMediaQuery`, the `types` map in `portableTextComponents.tsx`.

DO:

- Ship the module in a single commit with its generated types.
- Reuse `media.image`, `media.video`, `media.videoLoop` from `studio/schemas/objects/media/`.
- Project i18n fields as full `{ _key, _type, language, value }` arrays.
- Read i18n via `pickLocalizedString` / `pickLocalizedPortableTextBlocks`.

DON'T:

- Land schema without component (or vice versa).
- Write a TS type for the module by hand — it is `ModuleOf<"module.<id>">`.
- Register an inline module in only some of the three inline places.
- Index i18n arrays directly (`title[0].value`).
- `coalesce(field[language==$locale].value, ...)` in GROQ.
- Hand-edit `*.gen.ts` or `studio/schema.json`.
